<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phra Ong Mahawangsa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Mudzaffar Shah I of Kedah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phra Ong Mahawangsa was, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hikayat-merong-mahawangsa">Kedah Annals</a>, the ruler of Old Kedah who converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in 1136 and took the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Mudzaffar Shah. He is regarded as the founder of the Kedah Sultanate, whose line of rulers continues today, though the traditional date of his conversion cannot be confirmed.</p></div>
